WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.620
Should the US ease up on Visa requirements
for brainiacs

00:00:03.620 --> 00:00:05.740
and other tech oriented foreigners.

00:00:05.740 --> 00:00:10.560
One in four high tech startups in America
were founded by immigrants.

00:00:10.560 --> 00:00:14.180
These high skilled immigrants are job makers
not job takers.

00:00:14.180 --> 00:00:15.260
Politicians and pundits

00:00:15.260 --> 00:00:20.720
are always talking about the importance of
high tech foreigners for the US economy.

00:00:20.730 --> 00:00:25.230
But the fact of the matter is that low skilled
immigrants make equally vital contributions

00:00:25.230 --> 00:00:26.740
and here are 5 reasons why.

00:00:30.120 --> 00:00:33.280
Most Americans are not competitors of low-skilled
immigrants,

00:00:33.280 --> 00:00:34.879
they are actually their customers.

00:00:34.880 --> 00:00:37.140
They buy all kinds of services from them:

00:00:37.140 --> 00:00:43.140
House cleaning services, childcare services,
landscaping services, home construction services.

00:00:43.140 --> 00:00:45.559
If Americans can spend less on these services,

00:00:45.559 --> 00:00:48.079
they have more money in their pocket to spend
elsewhere,

00:00:48.080 --> 00:00:50.920
which means more jobs created elsewhere in
the economy.

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:58.740
The Latino and other foreign workers don't
have ties to the local community

00:00:58.740 --> 00:01:01.360
and they don't have invested in property.

00:01:01.360 --> 00:01:06.420
They can pick up their bags and leave at any
point to wherever they are needed.

00:01:06.420 --> 00:01:09.540
They can go to where houses are built in Arizona

00:01:09.550 --> 00:01:14.120
or they can go and pick fruit in Florida,
they can go wherever they want.

00:01:14.120 --> 00:01:17.860
They "grease the wheels" of an economy, as
one economist put it.

00:01:17.860 --> 00:01:21.160
They add to the resilience and dynamism of
the American economy.

00:01:24.170 --> 00:01:27.600
Another way in which low skilled immigrants
help the economy

00:01:27.600 --> 00:01:30.700
is by increasing the supply of high skilled
workers

00:01:30.700 --> 00:01:32.850
and these high-skilled workers are called
women.

00:01:32.850 --> 00:01:36.680
Many professional women would be forced to
spend much more time at home

00:01:36.680 --> 00:01:40.240
taking care of their children, cleaning, doing laundry

00:01:40.240 --> 00:01:46.520
if it were not for the presence of foreign nannies,
Korean dry cleaners or Chinese takeout.

00:01:49.680 --> 00:01:52.060
A big fear about low-skilled immigrants

00:01:52.060 --> 00:01:56.380
is because they are poor they impose a big
cost on the welfare state.

00:01:56.380 --> 00:01:58.940
But the truth is that most of them

00:01:58.940 --> 00:02:03.360
don't even qualify for most means tests benefits that Americans do.

00:02:03.360 --> 00:02:05.160
They don't qualify for food stamps,

00:02:05.160 --> 00:02:08.920
they don't qualify for all kinds of federal assistance programs.

00:02:08.920 --> 00:02:13.600
So in fact they might be saving the welfare
state money rather than costing it money.

00:02:16.820 --> 00:02:18.440
They create more jobs for Americans

00:02:18.440 --> 00:02:23.400
because they reduce the cost of a key import
in production which is labor.

00:02:23.400 --> 00:02:27.080
And when labor costs go down, more businesses
can form,

00:02:27.080 --> 00:02:31.520
and when more businesses can form, there are
more jobs for everyone--including Americans.

00:02:31.520 --> 00:02:36.040
The fact that there is somebody else to do
menial work like pulling weeds

00:02:36.040 --> 00:02:39.460
Americans can do relatively more value added
work.

00:02:39.460 --> 00:02:41.980
For instance, their English speaking skills

00:02:41.980 --> 00:02:46.520
become more marketable in a diverse economy
with lots of immigrants.

00:02:46.520 --> 00:02:49.200
These skills would have otherwise been taken
for granted

00:02:49.200 --> 00:02:53.300
but they become much more marketable and command
a premium in the labor market.

